From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:48:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add GPU and GMU nodes

Content from the A830 submission series (20260809-pakala-gpu, patch 3/6)
with the GMU at 0x3d37000/0x68000 per the stock erhai DT (the series'
0x3d6c000 does not match this hardware), plus the qfprom speed-bin cell.
GPU clock list follows the gmu.yaml binding for adreno-gmu-830.1.

Three GMU register windows exist for this part: mainline/the submission
series uses 0x3d6c000/0x32000, yzddmr6's tree (kept here) uses
0x3d37000/0x68000 as in the stock erhai DT, and the previous erhai port
used 0x3d6a000/0x35000. a6xx_gmu_init() derives gmu->mmio_offset from
the GMU window start relative to the GPU base and the gmu_read/write
helpers normalize by it, so register offsets resolve to the same
physical addresses whichever window start is used.

[Backport onto the erhai port: replace the port's gpu@3d00000 (0x40000
 window + cx_dbgc) and gmu@3d6a000 nodes with these; keep the port's
 zap-shader firmware-name "qcom/gen80000_zap.mbn"; leave the existing
 cooling-maps untouched; drop the erhai.dts &gmu_opp_table override,
 the 500/650 MHz table now lives in the dtsi.]

(cherry picked from commit 2112ee5f8313394e6afa9e1b4e700a54668d8ccd)
Link: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-erhai/commit/2112ee5f8313394e6afa9e1b4e700a54668d8ccd
Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
